1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,600
Your team moves fast.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,950
Your product context should keep up.

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:06,250
Requirements live in documents.

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,200
Changes arrive in conversations.

5
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:12,700
Your coding agent starts with whatever context someone remembered to paste.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,750
Orchestra connects the evidence, the decisions, and the work.

7
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,550
Start with a source.

8
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:23,125
Ask Socrates a product question, then open the citation behind its answer.

9
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:27,150
In our Northstar project, CSV export is documented.

10
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:29,650
PDF export is a request.

11
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:31,250
Those are different things.

12
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:34,550
Truth Inbox brings proposed changes into review.

13
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:37,600
Authorised decisions shape the Product Brain.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,200
Agent Preflight gives your coding agent a scoped context pack.

15
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,250
Postflight links reported work back to that starting point.

16
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:47,550
Keep the reason behind the requirement.

17
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:52,025
Give the next person, and the next agent, a clearer place to begin.

18
00:00:52,695 --> 00:00:53,700
Orchestra.

19
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,820
Product Brain for High Speed Teams.
